# Runtime state written by utils/file (per-world building records, etc.)
state/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Dev-only trees: scratch references and the legacy PalSmith code kept on disk for
# reference while porting.
#
# NEITHER Scripts/palforge/test/ NOR Scripts/palforge/tests/ IS HERE, and the second of those
# was a real defect rather than a judgement call. `Scripts/palforge/tests/` used to be listed on
# this line, and it is LIVE CODE: core/registry.lua requires `palforge.tests` and runs its 8
# checks at startup under dev, and `require("palforge.tests.catalog")` is the body of the
# `ps_catalog` console command registered in the same file. A clone therefore had a boot path
# and a console command pointing at four files the repository did not carry, and the install
# tree in the docs could not be right about it either. Both directories ship.
#
# /tests/ below is ROOT-anchored and is a different tree entirely — the Python/Mojo scratch
# harness at the repo root — so it stays ignored and does not reach anything under Scripts/.
tmp/
/tests/
deprecated/

